chocolatecake: Okay... Alright. Do you know what spacetime is?
- Skip basic explanation
	character: Like... the scientific stuff? The thing Einstein proposed?
	chocolatecake: Yes, that. The model around his theory of relativity, how space and time are linked. Basically just one long, flat plane in most models.
	jump basic explanation
- Hear basic explanation
	character: Uh... No.
	chocolatecake: Alright. Basically, there's a four dimensional... thing consisting of width, length and height, alongside time. Most diagrams are a flat plane with everything on it.
	character: Uh-huh.
	chocolatecake: So let's take the Sun. The Sun from now wouldn't be the Sun from 10,000 years ago. With the theory of spacetime, that point where the Sun was 10,000 years ago wouldn't be the same as it would be now, ignoring the fact that the Sun moves and all that.
	character: Uh...
	chocolatecake: That's because of time. If something stays in the exact same spot in space for 1,000 years, in a spacetime model, it would still be in a different position because of the difference in time.
	character: Okay. I... think I get it.
label basic explanation
character: What about it?
chocolatecake: I'm getting to that! So, you know that, using that model, denser objects like stars and planets weigh the plane down, creating gravity?
character: I do now.
character: What does this have to do with magic, and mana?
chocolatecake: Again, getting to it. So, those stars and planets are bending spacetime.
character: Uh-huh.
chocolatecake: All that magic is is imposing your human will onto spacetime and bending it like that.
character: ...Yeah, you've lost me.
chocolatecake: Okay- so! You have a conscious and subconscious will. It's what drives you to eat, drink, blink, all that.
character: Yeah.
chocolatecake: You can impose that will onto doing certain things. If you don't want to do something, but still do it, that's forcing your will to do something, or imposing it.
character: ...Yeah? How the hell does that make any sense with 'imposing your will to bend spacetime?'
chocolatecake: It's insane, right? Why else do you think wizards and mages are so few and far between? It's because they have abnormally strong wills, also known as Mana.
character: ...Oh.
character: Wait, but if someone can bend spacetime, wouldn't that just make gravity? How can they cast fireballs and stuff?
chocolatecake: The way that stars and planets bend spacetime to create gravity is simply a byproduct of their mass. By imposing a conscious will, you can alter how the bending takes form.
character: This is... insane. So, people can just control reality?
chocolatecake: What do you think wizards are? Just regular people?
character: ...Fair. So, how am I like this?
chocolatecake: You got struck with a spell, as you know.
character: Uh-huh.
chocolatecake: That spell was tailored to bring the target's most beloved into reality.
character: ...Sounds complex.
chocolatecake: It is. Incredibly so. So, with you being the target, that allows you to bring us into reality.
character: So... you never existed before tonight?
chocolatecake: ...Not exactly? It's hard to explain, and you look like you're about to have an aneurysm.
character: Yeah, I am. This is a sci-fi plot. My life was normal before all this, and now there's reality warpers and stuff!?
chocolatecake: You knew wizards existed before this.
character: Yeah! But I didn't know how they did their stuff! I just figured... I don't know what I figured, but it wasn't this.
chocolatecake: That's fine.
character: It's insane. I was having fun just cooking, and then this happened.
chocolatecake: Yeah.
character: It's... it doesn't...
chocolatecake: You wanted the explanation.
character: Yeah... Yeah. [shake amp=50 freq=2] Okay. I'm good. I'm fine, and I'm calm.
chocolatecake: Are you?
character: Better than ever.
chocolatecake: Good. That's enough for now.
jump cakeENDR/